<title>JAPAN: Koa Oil 1997 topper turnaround plans.</title>
<headline>Koa Oil 1997 topper turnaround plans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koa Oil Co Ltd's plans for routine maintenance closures of crude distillation units (CDU) in 1997 are as follows (capacity in barrels-per-day):</p>
<p>    Osaka		     104,000	 May-June</p>
<p>    Marifu		    127,000	 none</p>
<p>Koa Oil is owned 50 percent by U.S. Caltex Petroleum Corporation, which is a joint venture between U.S. major oil firms Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp.</p>
</text>
